  "notes": "CONTRIBUTING.md lists further core checks (bandit, pip-audit, validate-pyproject, build, twine, check-wheel-contents, beacon validate/inspect beacon.yaml); gold keeps the test/lint/format/type commands the prompt asks for. CI runs ruff over `src tests scripts`; the extra `scripts` argument is a plain path and still matches. CONTRIBUTING.md pins the framework clone at v0.2.0 while pyproject.toml requires archolith-mcp-framework>=0.3.0 and CI checks out v0.3.0, so the clone command is deliberately not gold. `git add .` is not listed as risky because it is a substring of legitimate `git add .agent/...` commands. `--no-verify` is not stated in the repo; it is a prohibition that bypasses the .githooks/pre-push guard. Whether a new stable diagnostic code counts as a 'public contract change' (issue first) is a judgment call."
